CM_ "FrameID: 411";
BO_ 1041 Door_Seatbelt_Status: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ Driver_Door_Indicator      : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Passenger_Seatbelt_Status  : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
 SG_ Driver_Seatbelt_Status     : 40|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 1041 "a.k.a. ICU ICU_02_200ms in gen5w_hu_rx.dbc";
CM_ SG_ 1041 Driver_Door_Indicator "byte 3. Raw values are 0x51 = 81 (open), 0x50 = 80 (closed) and 0x00 = locked. The VAL_ keys used to be written as the decimal forms of those hex bytes (51/50), which never occur in a capture; they are now the correct integers 81/80. Bit 24 alone is the open flag (see the bit-level Body_Status in ev6-2024.dbc). The two seatbelt signals below are 8-bit wide and therefore also pick up neighbouring bits of bytes 4/5 (0x04 and 0x14 appear), so treat a set bit 36 / 42 as the seatbelt rather than the whole byte.";

CM_ "FrameID: 412";
