CM_ "Probably wrong: unsigned int, and this byte doesn't change in my logs. --TRH";
BO_ 550 Ambient_Temperature: 8 Vector__XXX
 SG_ Outdoor_Temperature : 24|8@1+ (1,-40) [-40|215] "C" Vector__XXX
CM_ BO_ 550 "a.k.a. CLU CLU_02_100ms_1 in gen5w_hu_rx.dbc";
CM_ SG_ 550 Outdoor_Temperature "byte 3. The bit placement matches the official CLU_OutTempCSta (24|8@1+ (1,-40) [-40|215]) in BO_ 549 CLU_02_100ms of dbcs/dbcs/HMVS4_CAN-FD_DBC_3Gen_R3_rev2.dbc:178, whose VAL_ makes 0..100 = -40..60 C, 101..254 = Reserved and 255 = Invalid. Every Ioniq 5 capture on disk (old/ and current folders, M-CAN and I-CAN) reads 0xFF = 255 = Invalid in this byte, so the -40 offset reports a nonsense 215 C unless 255 is treated as no-data. Bytes 4-7 carry session-stable values of unknown meaning, so a real ambient value may live there instead; unresolved.";
VAL_ 550 Outdoor_Temperature 255 "Invalid" ;

